From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: A733's BXM-4-64 MC1 is a known GPU

The mainline driver's allowlist is three BVNCs and ours is not one of them, so
on A733 it refuses to bind:

  powervr 1800000.gpu: [drm] *ERROR* Unknown GPU! Set 'exp_hw_support' to bypass

The board boots with a working GPU only because the command line carries
powervr.exp_hw_support=1, and the driver then announces "Running on unknown
hardware; expect issues" on every boot. This adds BVNC 36.56.104.183.

WHAT HANGS ON AN ALLOWLIST ENTRY: NOTHING BUT THE NUMBER.

That was the question worth answering before touching this, and it was answered
by reading the driver, not by assuming. pvr_gpu_support_level()
(pvr_device.c:529) is a switch of bodyless case labels; its only caller,
pvr_check_gpu_supported(), prints a message and returns -ENODEV. There is no
BVNC-indexed feature table in the kernel at all: features, BRN quirks and ERN
enhancements arrive as bitmasks and a parameter array read out of the FIRMWARE
FILE, in pvr_fw_get_device_info() (pvr_fw.c:167). The BVNC itself is used in
exactly three further places -- building the firmware filename, checking it
against the firmware header, and reporting it to userspace through
DRM_PVR_DEV_QUERY_GPU_INFO_GET, which is the number Mesa looks up in its own
table.

WHY "SUPPORTED" AND NOT "EXPERIMENTAL"

Two reasons, and the second is the operative one.

(1) Our firmware was compared byte for byte against 36.52.104.182, which
upstream promoted to supported in e55fead22ff9. Both files were parsed and laid
side by side: identical feature mask, identical 29 parameter values, identical
ERN set, identical FW build. The device info differs in ONE bit -- .182 carries
BRN 71242, we do not -- and cmp finds 5 differing bytes in the whole 128 KiB.
BRN 71242 is used once in the driver and is additionally gated on
!gpu_multicore_support, a feature our firmware sets. There is no behavioural
difference to a core upstream already calls supported.

(2) PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL would change nothing operationally: read
pvr_check_gpu_supported() and it returns -ENODEV for EXPERIMENTAL without
exp_hw_support, exactly as for UNKNOWN. The choice is between this and the
status quo; "experimental" is not a middle position the code offers.

⚠ WHAT THIS IS NOT: an upstream submission. Upstream's stated evidence for
promoting .182 was a Vulkan CTS 1.4.5.3 run on real hardware. We have a GL
acceptance that renders 65536 of 65536 pixels exactly (on the board) and no CTS
run, and rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw is not in linux-firmware -- it exists only in
Imagination's fork. The first upstream step is that firmware MR, not this patch.
Recorded so nobody mistakes a tree-local entry for an upstream position.

Three hunks, not the two an "entry" suggests: upstream's e55fead22ff9 only MOVED
.182 between branches, so its MODULE_FIRMWARE line already existed. Ours is a
new BVNC and needs its own.

BVNC provenance: read from the silicon on the 8 GiB board (ROGUE_CR_CORE_ID__PBVNC via
pvr_load_gpu_id), and independently from the firmware header of the file the
driver loads.

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -533,6 +533,7 @@
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(33, 15, 11, 3):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 52, 104, 182):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
+	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 56, 104, 183):
 		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
 	default:
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
  * * AXE-1-16M (33.15.11.3)
  * * BXM-4-64 MC1 (36.52.104.182)
  * * BXS-4-64 MC1 (36.53.104.796)
+ * * BXM-4-64 MC1 (36.56.104.183)
  */
 
 /**
@@ -1537,3 +1538,4 @@
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_33.15.11.3_v1.fw");
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.52.104.182_v1.fw");
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.53.104.796_v1.fw");
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw");
